Let's perform direct substitution and see what happens!

$\begin{align}
f\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)&=\dfrac{1-\sin^2\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)}{\cos\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{3}}\right)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1-\left( \dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)^2}{\left( \dfrac{1}{2}\right)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{2}
\end{align}$
